il'].replace('Every clue JSON still shows current_role: analyst;','Every clue JSON (still on D14/D15) shows current_role: analyst;')\nby['bopla-field-read']['detail']=\"D14 showed the property-level read side through an explicit `fields`+`action` pair on an inventory-listed route (seen, handler exists). Remaining sibling: routes WITHOUT an inventory where hidden keys come back through ?fields=*, ?include=all, ?expand=*, ?view=admin|full|debug, ?debug=1, Accept: application/vnd.api+json, or list endpoints returning keys the HTML omits (secret, proof, note, internal). Compare key sets against the page. Parser: proof regex after JSON flattening.\"\nby['bopla-field-read']['priority']=2\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"ssrf-filter-bypass\",\"concept\":\"SSRF sequels: filtered host/scheme, redirect, file://, blind (row 12b)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D15 was the plain form (feature?url=http://127.0.0.1:8080<internal_only route>; port 80 -> fetch_failed). Sequels in the D10->D11 / D03->D12 style: blocklist on 127.0.0.1/localhost -> 2130706433, 0x7f000001, 017700000001, 127.1, 127.0.0.1.nip.io-style only if the app names it, [::1], [::ffff:127.0.0.1], 0.0.0.0; allowlist 'must start with/contain <host>' -> https://<allowed>@127.0.0.1:8080/, http://127.0.0.1:8080#@<allowed>, ?u=<allowed>; scheme filter -> file:///run/huntress/objective.txt, FILE://, gopher only if named; redirect hop via an app-owned open redirect (row 24b) or a clue route that 302s; POST/JSON body {url} when GET 405s; port ladder 8080, 80, 5000, 8000, 3000, 8888, 9000 from error hints. Parser: proof regex in the proxied body, base64/JSON-wrapped content fields. Fixture: D15 error bodies (absolute_url_required, internal_only, fetch_failed) + a mocked blocked_host.\"},\n {\"id\":\"api-shadow-version\",\"concept\":\"improper API inventory: shadow / deprecated / beta endpoint skips the check (row 39, OWASP API9)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D13-D15 walked the OWASP API Top 10 (API3, API5, API7) and D14's prompt said 'take inventory of every endpoint'. Planner: from /api/inventory, /openapi.json, /swagger.json, /api-docs, /v2/api-docs, /api/clues and JS literals, collect every path; emit version swaps (/api/v2/x -> /api/v1/x, /api/x -> /api/v0|beta|internal|legacy|old/x), `X-API-Version: 1`, `?version=1`, `Accept: application/vnd.<app>.v1+json`; call the protected operation (protected_reference / admin route) on each. Parser: proof regex; 403 on the current version + 200 on the shadow = the bug.\"},\n {\"id\":\"api-resource-limit-overread\",\"concept\":\"unrestricted resource consumption / pagination over-read (row 40, OWASP API4)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"List routes with limit/page_size/per_page/offset/page: plan limit=1000|100000|-1|0, page=0|-1, offset beyond the public window, size=all, and batch/array ids (id=1,2,3 / ids[]=). Look for records past the public set carrying proof/secret. No flooding: <= 10 requests.\"},\n {\"id\":\"api-unsafe-consumption\",\"concept\":\"app trusts a third-party / webhook / callback response (OWASP API10)\",\"priority\":3,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Routes that import from a URL or accept a webhook payload and then act on the content (e.g. 'sync profile from partner'): point at an app-owned echo/paste route or a data: URL we control, return JSON with role/admin/redirect fields; chains with SSRF (row 12) and mass assignment (row 9). Parser: proof regex on the follow-up secondary route.\"},\n]\n# re-rank: priority 1 list\nfor gid in ('prototype-pollution',): by[gid]['priority']=1\nby['prototype-pollution']['detail']+=\" Raised to 1 after D15: the API run (D13 mass assignment -> D14 property authz) keeps the JSON-object-binding family hot and Node costumes recur.\"\nG=G[:2]+[x for x in G[2:] if x['priority']==1]+new[:2]+[x for x in G[2:] if x['priority']!=1]+new[2:]\nG=sorted(G,key=lambda g:g['priority'])  # stable\nids=[g['id'] for g in G]; assert len(ids)==len(set(ids))\ntxt=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in G)+\"\\n]\"\njson.loads(txt)\ns=s[:a]+txt+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"decoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built (no web prebuild lane). Dropped after D13:\n`ssti-engine-probe` (seen D11), `port-day22-handlers` (csrf/upload now in lib/web/handlers); mass assignment (seen\nD13) removed from `role-tamper-planner`, second-order SQLi (seen D12) from `sqli-union-blind`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"decoy. \"note\" = harness/prompt change. \"tool\" = install. None built (no web prebuild lane, no `web:*` keys in\n.run/prebuild-state.json). Dropped after D13: `ssti-engine-probe` (seen D11), `port-day22-handlers`. Dropped after\nD15: `ssrf-planner` (seen D15; replaced by `ssrf-filter-bypass`); D14's inventory field x action read folded into\n`bopla-field-read` (now the no-inventory sibling). Added after D15: `ssrf-filter-bypass`, `api-shadow-version`,\n`api-resource-limit-overread`, `api-unsafe-consumption`.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint(sum(1 for g in G if g['action']=='prebuild'), [ (g['id'],g['priority']) for g in G])\nEOF\nwc -l reference/coverage/web.md reference/techniques/web.md; git diff --stat -- reference/"}}}
